spec se02-straggler-holds-frontier: 2 sessions, 2 permutations
# SE02. s0 writes s and reserves its commit instant without publishing it (the commit
# hold, the straggler). s1 then commits t1 through a cypher.Session (autocommit CREATE): the commit acknowledges without
# waiting on s0. A sessionless read excludes t1 (the frontier is held below it), and
# in_flight_commits is 2. s1's session read waits in the background for its own
# commit (sessions_waiting = 1) and returns only when s0 publishes; then s's write and
# t1 become visible in one step (F11). The control interleaving publishes s0 first.

starting permutation: s0w s0a s1w s1lag s1fr s1aw s1wait s0p s1rel s1seen
step s0w: lpg: SetNodeProperty(s, v, 1)
step s0a: lpg: Graph.AllocateCommitTS (instant reserved, not published)
step s1w: <cypher.Session, deadline 30s> CREATE (n:N {name:'t1', v:1}) RETURN n.name AS name
name
----
"t1"
(1 row)
step s1lag: <sessionless> MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name, n.v AS v ORDER BY name
name|v
----+-
"s" |0
(1 row)
step s1fr: <MVCCStats: in_flight_commits, sessions_waiting>
in_flight_commits|sessions_waiting
-----------------+----------------
2                |0               
(1 row)
step s1aw: <start cypher.Session in the background> MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name, n.v AS v ORDER BY name
step s1wait: <background wait: sessions_waiting, returned>
sessions_waiting|returned
----------------+--------
1               |false   
(1 row)
step s0p: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s1rel: <collect the background statement's rows>
name|v
----+-
"s" |1
"t1"|1
(2 rows)
step s1seen: <sessionless> MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name, n.v AS v ORDER BY name
name|v
----+-
"s" |1
"t1"|1
(2 rows)
final ffr: <MVCCStats: in_flight_commits, sessions_waiting>
in_flight_commits|sessions_waiting
-----------------+----------------
0                |0               
(1 row)

